@startuml
title SEQ-01 - Mailbox proof, password recovery and OAuth
autonumber
actor User
boundary Client as "Web / Chrome"
control Core
database CoreDB as "PostgreSQL core"
participant Mail as "Resend / mailbox"
participant OAuth as "Google / Facebook"
User -> Client: Choose registration, login or recovery
alt Registration / resend
  Client -> Core: POST /auth/register or /resend-verification
  Core -> CoreDB: Validate application; reserve scoped HMAC challenge + limits
  Core -> Mail: Deliver short-lived code to eligible mailbox
  Core --> Client: 202 accepted; no identity or tokens
  Mail --> User: Six-digit code
  User -> Client: Code + chosen password + confirmation
  Client -> Core: POST /auth/verify-email {email,code,password}
  Core -> CoreDB: Lock; check scope, expiry, attempts and HMAC
  alt Invalid proof
    Core -> CoreDB: Commit failed-attempt counter
    Core --> Client: EMAIL_CODE_INVALID
  else Valid proof
    Core -> CoreDB: Atomically create/verify user, set password, consume codes, revoke old sessions
    Core --> Client: 204; return to login
  end
else Forgot password
  Client -> Core: POST /auth/forgot-password {email}
  Core -> CoreDB: Reserve challenge for active password account; generic response
  Core -> Mail: Send recovery code when eligible
  Core --> Client: 202 accepted
  User -> Client: Code + new password + confirmation
  Client -> Core: POST /auth/reset-password
  Core -> CoreDB: Atomically validate/consume code, update password, revoke all sessions
  Core --> Client: 204; explicit login required
else Password login
  Client -> Core: POST /auth/login {email,password}
  Core -> CoreDB: Lock scoped user and load credential
  Core -> Core: Verify password; require active verified email
  alt Unverified
    Core --> Client: EMAIL_VERIFICATION_REQUIRED
  else Verified
    Core -> CoreDB: Create refresh session
    Core --> Client: Safe user + access/refresh tokens
  end
else OAuth
  Client -> OAuth: Interactive provider flow
  OAuth --> Client: Provider token
  Client -> Core: POST /auth/google or /facebook
  Core -> OAuth: Verify audience, expiry, subject and email
  Core -> CoreDB: Resolve scoped identity; remove unverified planted password on linking
  Core -> CoreDB: Create session
  Core --> Client: Safe user + access/refresh tokens
end
note over Core,CoreDB
Codes are application/email/purpose scoped, short-lived and single-use.
Wrong attempts persist. Protected access checks stored session revocation.
No identity, password, OTP or session is trusted from client metadata.
end note
@enduml
